"""Create the ``leads`` table (Requirements 13.1, 13.6, 13.7, 13.11).

One migration, one table. Every bound of design §4.3 arrives as a named
``CHECK`` and the two normalization columns of §3.6.5 arrive as
``GENERATED ALWAYS AS (…) STORED``, so the constraint layer is deployed by the
same statement that creates the table — there is no window in which a writer
meets these columns without the rules that bound them.

Deliberately **not** here, so a reviewer does not go looking:

* the nine ``leads`` indexes of §4.7, including the two over the generated
  columns and the ``gin_trgm_ops`` search index — task 2.4;
* every other table of Requirement 13.5 — tasks 2.2 and 2.3;
* the ten triggers of §4.6 — tasks 3.1 to 3.4. ``scripts/check_deferred_activations.py``
  greps the migrations directory for trigger-creating DDL to decide when task
  3.5's ``migrations`` pytest marker is overdue, so this file must contain no
  such statement — and, since the check is a plain text search, must not spell
  one out in prose either.
"""

